      en: ["Often cited as the second oldest mosque in the Maldives.", "Built in the 12th century by Sultan Mohammed bin Abdullah.", "Utilizes materials reclaimed from pre-Islamic Buddhist structures.", "Located in the center of Nilandhoo island in Faafu Atoll.", "Renowned for its archaic and robust coral stone construction.", "The adjacent cemetery contains gravestones spanning several centuries."],
      es: ["Construida en 1159 d.C.", "Dimensiones: 18 m de largo, 10 m de ancho", "Minbar de madera de 3 m de altura", "Muros de coral de 60 cm de espesor", "Techo renovado cada 5 años", "Restaurada en 2005"],
